  "slug": "basal-ganglia-29a7",
  "summary": "New brain atlases and tools standardize data and map cell-type regulation across disease, development and connectivity, making cross-study reuse and interpretation easier.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is resources and tools that place brain cell-type-resolved molecular data in disease, developmental or anatomical context. A harmonized set of wild-type and Alzheimer's disease model mouse sc/snRNA-seq datasets standardizes sample annotations for reuse. A multi-omic QTL atlas from 231 human prefrontal cortex donors links disorder genetic risk to cell-type and developmental regulation, and scCVD integrates scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq across 701 samples and over 4.68 million cells for cerebrovascular disease. Tool-oriented work extends interpretation to other layers: SCOUBI maps axon-dendrite interfaces from extrasomatic RNA in mouse spatial transcriptomics, VEGABrain projects bulk RNA-seq onto developing human brain atlas surfaces with ssGSEA enrichment maps, and CSDX relates human gene expression to mouse connectome strength. Tissue, species and modality differ across these works.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
